# Untracked files copied into every new worktree.
#
# A worktree is a fresh checkout of tracked files and nothing else, so anything
# .gitignore covers is simply absent from it -- and the failure looks like the
# tool being broken rather than the file being missing.
#
# settings.local.json is this machine's permission mode. Without it a new
# worktree falls back to the default, and the protocol's own writes start being
# refused: measured 2026-08-15, `git add` was allowed in one worktree and denied
# in the next one cut minutes later, for no reason visible from inside either.
.claude/settings.local.json
